WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.612
This slide shows the transition from Module 3 to
Module 4 In

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:10.150
Module 3 most of our questions returned individual
records For example we

00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:15.450
could retrieve one patient row filter admissions or
update one record Module

00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:18.962
4 asks us to summarize many rows into information
that is easier

00:00:18.988 --> 00:00:23.250
to interpret Think about a sales table with hundreds
or thousands of

00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:28.988
transactions A decision-maker may not want to read
every transaction They

00:00:29.012 --> 00:00:32.950
may want total revenue by category average sale
price or the number

00:00:32.962 --> 00:00:38.312
of unique products sold Aggregation converts the
detailed rows into that higher-level

00:00:38.325 --> 00:00:43.725
view The workflow on this slide is very important We
still begin

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.938
with detail Then we decide the grain of the output
Next we

00:00:48.962 --> 00:00:53.500
choose the measure such as a count total or average
After that

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.775
we decide whether any source rows should be filtered
before grouping and

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.750
whether any summary groups should be filtered after
grouping Finally we validate

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:06.262
the result That last step matters because an
aggregate can look reasonable

00:01:06.288 --> 00:01:10.550
even when the grouping or filtering logic is wrong A
useful habit

00:01:10.562 --> 00:01:13.862
is to compare the summary back to the source rows
especially when

00:01:13.888 --> 00:01:17.862
building a new report So the main idea is simple do
not

00:01:17.875 --> 00:01:21.675
start with GROUP BY just because you want a summary
Start with

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.438
the question and define what one result row should
mean
